  "limits": [
    "Native server is a deterministic Node stdio LSP fixture, not the actual TypeScript language server, rust-analyzer or gopls. Its child RSS cannot establish whole-app RAM savings or real project indexing cost.",
    "Editor document and undo objects intentionally remain mounted. This change releases language-server ownership and background validation, not all visited-pane state.",
    "Immediate release can trade memory for cold server initialization/reindexing; hardware/project-specific latency and an evidence-based grace policy remain open.",
    "VS Code disposal is covered by its stand-in integration, not a live installed VS Code runtime. Webview reload without disposal and renderer crash were not separately exercised. Packaged and cross-platform runs remain open.",
    "Native snapshots predate the final resolved-URI alias refinement. nativeSourceSha256 records their exact sources; sourceSha256 records the final unit/integration-verified sources."
